/*
.DS_Store

# Included list
!arch/
!clangd/
!ghostty/
!githooks/
!lib/
!nvim/
!tmux/
!zsh/
!notifier/
!.ideavimrc
!claude/
!ai/
!codex/
!homebrew/
!hypr/
!windows/
!omarchy/
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!bootstrap.sh

# ghostty / tmux — machine-local overrides, same convention as zsh/private.sh
ghostty/private.conf
tmux/private.conf

# nvim
nvim/.claude/
nvim/*.log
nvim/lua/private/*
!nvim/lua/private/README.md

# tmux
tmux/plugins/

# zsh
zsh/*
!zsh/.zshrc
!zsh/custom
zsh/**/.git

# claude
claude/memory/private/
claude/MEMORY.private.md
claude/*.lock
claude/*.tmp
claude/.claude

# notifier
notifier/macos/AgentNotifier
notifier/linux/agent-notifier
notifier/linux/agent-notifier-send

# codex — site-local sensitive patterns (never committed)
codex/scripts/sensitive-patterns.local

# homebrew — track Brewfile + bootstrap.sh, not Brewfile.lock.json or dumps
homebrew/*
!homebrew/Brewfile
!homebrew/bootstrap.sh

# windows — build output and machine-local overrides
windows/dist/
windows/private.ps1

# omarchy — the theme templates, and so far only those. themed/*.tpl is
# hand-written and machine-independent, and losing it fails silently: a missing
# template just drops the prompt back to Omarchy's stock starship config with
# no error. The .sample alongside it ships with the omarchy package, so *.tpl
# deliberately does not match it.
#
# The directory is opened one pattern at a time because most of what Omarchy
# keeps here is reproducible without us — shell.json and
# extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc are byte-identical to the package defaults,
# every hooks/*.hook also exists under /usr/share/omarchy, and plugins/ and
# themes/ are empty.
#
# branding/*.txt and shell.toml were open questions; both are settled now, and
# both stay out.
#
# branding/about.txt and branding/screensaver.txt do have package defaults,
# under other names — omarchy-branding-{about,screensaver} reset copies
# $OMARCHY_PATH/icon.txt and logo.txt over them, which is why searching for the
# same filename found nothing. The files here are byte-identical to those
# (md5 d1472bfb… and 4f14293d…), so nothing has been customised and `omarchy
# branding about reset` reproduces them. Revisit if `omarchy branding about
# image` is ever used: transcoding a chosen PNG makes a file no default can
# restore.
#
# shell.toml is written by omarchy-display-text-size, the same command that
# rewrites font-size in ghostty/config — it holds `[font] base-size`, this
# monitor's DPI and nothing else. Tracking it would push one machine's text
# size onto every other, which is what the clean filter in
# lib/git-filter-machine-local.sh exists to prevent for the ghostty half.
# default/themed/shell.toml.tpl also rewrites it on theme changes, so it is
# closer to a generated file than a config.
omarchy/*
!omarchy/themed/
omarchy/themed/*
!omarchy/themed/*.tpl

# hypr — the hand-edited Hyprland config, minus what belongs to this monitor.
#
# Only bindings.lua differs from the packaged defaults today, but the others are
# tracked too: they are the files Omarchy expects to be edited, and having them
# already under version control is what makes the next edit show up as a diff
# rather than as a surprise. `omarchy refresh config hypr/<file>` restores any
# of them from the package.
#
# monitors.lua is excluded. Its only change is omarchy_monitor_scale = 1.6,
# which is this 4K panel and nothing else — the same reason omarchy/shell.toml
# and the ghostty font-size line stay out of git. Tracking it would hand one
# display's scale to every other machine.
hypr/*
!hypr/*.lua
!hypr/*.conf
hypr/monitors.lua
hypr/*.bak.*
